  "Number": 34,
  "Question": "When the circumference of a toy balloon is increased from \\(20\\) inches to \\(25\\) inches, the radius is increased by:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(5\\) in",
    "B": "\\(2\\dfrac12\\) in",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac5\\pi\\) in",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{2\\pi}\\) in",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{\\pi}{5}\\) in"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "For a circle with circumference \\(C\\) and radius \\(r\\), \\(C=2\\pi r\\), so \\(r=C/(2\\pi)\\). Therefore the increase in radius is\n\\[\n\\frac{25}{2\\pi}-\\frac{20}{2\\pi}\n=\\frac{5}{2\\pi}\\text{ inches}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
